    "notes": "The main Holy Virgin church includes its open chambers, restored masonry and visitor stair. The five northern chapel and cell groups have separate cliff faces and modeled cavities based on published photographs and mapped path endpoints. Cliff relief, portal dimensions and interior layouts are reconstructed visually. The painted bands and figures suggest surviving pigments and their arrangement without reproducing individual scenes. The local rock meshes join the viewer’s standard terrain. Their cutouts apply only on the immediate cliff patches and preserve mapped paths, water and surrounding landscape."
